## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design for data drift in a globally distributed system, emphasizing data quality governance, region-specific containment, and systematic problem resolution.

## Key Concepts
- Data drift detection and distribution monitoring across geographic regions
- CAPA data model with comprehensive evidence capture and drift scoring
- Region-aware lifecycle management with rollback capabilities
- Lightweight REST API for auditability and traceability
- Structured RCA methodology and controlled canary deployment

## Code Example
```javascript
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  region: string;
  evidence: string[];
  telemetry: Record<string, any>;
  driftScore: number;
  supplierVersion: string;
  status: 'detected' | 'containment' | 'resolution' | 'prevention';
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ability to design a CAPA for ML drift in a real-time system with multi-region considerations, plus practical data modeling and API design.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model with evidence and region
- Lifecycle state machine for CAPA progression
- Minimal REST API endpoints for create/update
- Region-aware metrics and canary remediation
- RCA templating for root-cause communication

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal API sketch
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  // create CAPA with fields from req.body
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'CAPA-001' });
});
```

